{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation","id":1507681,"title":"Sorcery and Vitae enhancement / distillation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-07T07:06:02-07:00","id":1507681,"title":"Sorcery and Vitae enhancement / distillation","content":"<b><i>Thought exercise. Not ( necessarily ) intended to be used in real games.</i></b><br /> <br /> In your opinion, according to RAI ( the &quot;spirit&quot; of the rules ) would it be possible for an hedge mage / low mage / sorcerer ( sourcebooks: wod - Sorcerer and Sorcerer - revised ) to use the linear magic - the Path of Alchemy or a similar Path like Herbalism / Brewing - to refine / distillate / somewhat obtain a more powerful ( in game terms, lower Generation ) Vitae from a larger quantity of weaker Vitae?<br /> <br /> Another idea: there's the Path of Enchantment which allows to create &quot;talismans&quot; ( in pratice, magic items ). Mabye a sorcerer could create an enchanted urn or chalice, or enchanted alambics, vials and other alchemic implements, to be used in order to refine the Vitae ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 04-07-2023, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T07:43:58-07:00","id":1507685,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's certainly possible.<br /> <br /> What you're asking about is the equivalent of a lonnger-lasting(if on vampire) and/or slightly altered(if on distilled vitae) version of the 3rd level of path of blood(blood of potency). This is certainly within the capabilities of the 5th dot of Alchemy in M20 sorcery.<br /> <br /> It's even More possible in earlier edition where legendary alchemist could straight up make artificial vampirism, awakening and first changes.<br /> <br /> That's before we get into the fact that V20 dark ages let's hedge sorcerers straight up learn blood magic and that the asamite &quot;From Mardukes Throat&quot;(permanently lower generation) is a 5th dot ritual in V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 04-07-2023, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T07:47:46-07:00","id":1507686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507685#post1507685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's even More possible in earlier edition where legendary alchemist could straight up make artificial vampirism, awakening and first changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon?<br /> I think I read most publications but I didn't remember reading this kind of things.<br /> May I ask what supplements we are talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T07:49:49-07:00","id":1507687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507686#post1507686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pardon?<br /> I think I read most publications but I didn't remember reading this kind of things.<br /> May I ask what supplements we are talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer revised, the 6th dot power for alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T08:14:23-07:00","id":1507689,"title":"","content":"I know this may have nothing to do with your question, but I remember that my ST once did a campaign where a Tremere did something similar to generate a type of bloodstone that was nothing more than concentrated and solidified vitae, which could be used in place of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T08:37:38-07:00","id":1507691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507689#post1507689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this may have nothing to do with your question, but I remember that my ST once did a campaign where a Tremere did something similar to generate a type of bloodstone that was nothing more than concentrated and solidified vitae, which could be used in place of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, your ST had players running around looking for forbidden artifacts only for the grand prize to be tremere blood skittles( <b>Principal Focus of Vitae Infusion, </b>a level 1 ritual)?<br /> <br /> That's Evil... I love it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 04-07-2023, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T11:12:48-07:00","id":1507702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507691#post1507691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, your ST had players running around looking for forbidden artifacts only for the grand prize to be tremere blood skittles( <b>Principal Focus of Vitae Infusion, </b>a level 1 ritual)?<br /> <br /> That's Evil... I love it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember the details, as it was years ago, but it must not be what you're thinking, this stone was supposed to be a blood substitute that a vampire could carry around and fill their blood pool just by breaking it in their mouth, In the end he dismissed this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T11:47:29-07:00","id":1507703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507702#post1507702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't remember the details, as it was years ago, but it must not be what you're thinking, this stone was supposed to be a blood substitute that a vampire could carry around and fill their blood pool just by breaking it in their mouth, In the end he dismissed this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Functions exactly the same as the tremere blood skittles ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T23:36:09-07:00","id":1507743,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the &quot;blood stone&quot; idea is just the Level 1 Blood Skittles ritual (which is what I'll call it from now on).<br /> <br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand, I would absolutely allow a Sorcerer with Alchemy/Herbalism/Advanced Chemistry 5 to refine Vitae into a stronger form.<br /> <br /> It would probably require a great deal of time, effort, and reagents to accomplish this distillation of Vitae. To the point it wouldn't be practical for normal Vampire consumption. But it could be done, if there was some specific reason for it. Maybe as an emergency boost for a Vampire, or for some arcane purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T10:33:48-07:00","id":1507946,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a blood sorcery Ritual that allows Assamites to collect and pool blood to then lower their generation? If I recall correctly there is a couple different versions and one of them has a process to make &quot;artificial low gen blood&quot; to lower your generation.<br /> <br /> Theoretically this could mean that a similar process could be made for human sorcery or to refine blood in particular. I'd probably allow it but it would be something really high. Top level magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T11:23:07-07:00","id":1507948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507946#post1507946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a blood sorcery Ritual that allows Assamites to collect and pool blood to then lower their generation? If I recall correctly there is a couple different versions and one of them has a process to make &quot;artificial low gen blood&quot; to lower your generation.<br /> <br /> Theoretically this could mean that a similar process could be made for human sorcery or to refine blood in particular. I'd probably allow it but it would be something really high. Top level magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>From marduke's throat. Mentioned above.<br /> <br /> It's a level 5 ritual, so if the ST is using Dark Ages rules any human can learn it because blood magic is capped at 5 dots for them(and can be used with sacrifices rather than vampire Vitae). Dark ages doesn't consider blood magic a &quot;Discipline&quot;, it treats it more like a basterdized version of mortal sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T23:54:57-07:00","id":1508002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507681-sorcery-and-vitae-enhancement-distillation?p=1507743#post1507743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would probably require a great deal of time, effort, and reagents to accomplish this distillation of Vitae. To the point it wouldn't be practical for normal Vampire consumption. But it could be done, if there was some specific reason for it. Maybe as an emergency boost for a Vampire, or for some arcane purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae refined or changed in this way could be used as a substance in regard to which Vitae ( or blood ) evaluations and comparisons would be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}